(EXP-56: values are converted between types with `as` or with `in`.
 Also covers: EXP-57 the `as a <type>` syntax, EXP-58 the article-free
 `as <type>` syntax being equivalent to it, EXP-59 the `<value> in <unit>`
 syntax existing at all.
 `in` is only legal on a timer's duration or elapsed, so the `in` line here is
 a timer one; EXP-88 records what happens on a plain number. The wait is a
 whole second so the recorded elapsed does not straddle a boundary.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox EXP-56.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   10
   10
   3.9
   3.9
   1
)
a text called tally is "10".
Print tally as a number.
Print tally as number.
Print 3.9 as a float.
Print 3.9 as float.
a timer called benchmark.
Start the benchmark.
Wait 1 second.
Stop the benchmark.
Print the benchmark's duration in seconds.
